+/// point in the list where the Pokemon *is* in its base form:
+///   * `taking: true` is the FIRST instruction Transform emits, so on apply the
+///     Pokemon is still untransformed, and on reverse every later mutation has
+///     already been undone.
+///   * `taking: false` is the LAST instruction the switch-out revert emits, so
